  {
   "id": "spacex-q3",
   "headline": "SpaceX's AI unit drives a 161% revenue jump",
   "facts": [
    "Q3 revenue $14.575bn, +161% y/y",
    "AI segment $7.56bn, +830%",
    "Net income $4.4bn vs -$1.1bn",
    "Capex $19.6bn, $16.4bn to AI",
    "~$1bn from Bitcoin recovery and related-party income (TechCrunch, single-source)"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1181412/000162828026066482/spaceexplorationtechnologi.htm",
    "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/20/spacexs-ai-business-is-beating-expectations/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "A quarterly report is just a scoreboard: money in, money out, and where it came from. SpaceX's third quarter shows revenue of $14.575bn, up 161% from $5.576bn a year earlier, and the biggest slice is now its AI segment at $7.56bn, up 830%, ahead of Starlink connectivity at $5.248bn and space at $1.767bn. Net income was $4.4bn against a $1.1bn loss before. The catch is cost: capital spending, meaning money put into equipment, hit $19.6bn, with $16.4bn going to AI. How solid is the profit? One outlet, TechCrunch, says about $1bn of revenue came from a Bitcoin recovery and related-party income, and no analyst expectations or share-price reaction were found.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "merger-committees",
   "headline": "Tesla and SpaceX boards study a merger",
   "facts": [
    "Special committees formed at both boards",
    "Musk excluded as conflicted",
    "Needs 50% of all Tesla shares",
    "No terms agreed",
    "$3.6tn combined value (The Verge, single-source)"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.theverge.com/science/1014984/spacex-tesla-merger-elon-musk-special-committees",
    "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/20/spacex-and-tesla-boards-form-special-committees-to-review-merger/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "A merger means two companies becoming one, and nothing here is agreed yet. On SpaceX's results call, Elon Musk said the boards of Tesla and SpaceX have each formed special committees of independent directors to review a possible merger, after shareholders asked. Musk is excluded as \"a conflicted party\". He called it \"a good idea\" but not a certainty, citing AI software, chip design, robotics and orbital data centres. A Tesla deal would need approval from 50% of all Tesla shares, not only those that vote, which he called \"quite a high hurdle\". The Verge, a single source, puts a combined value at \"upwards of $3.6 trillion\". No terms exist, so the outcome is open.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "deepseek-ban",
   "headline": "US removes DeepSeek from federal civilian systems",
   "facts": [
    "DHS order, Federal Register 2026-21447, public 19 Oct",
    "Procurement ban and removal from civilian IT",
    "Defence excluded; effective end July per BBC (single-source)",
    "China foreign ministry objected 20 Oct"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents/2026-21447.json",
    "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjkgeq0k1wevo",
    "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/20/us-orders-federal-agencies-to-remove-chinas-deepseek-ai-from-their-systems/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "DeepSeek is a Chinese AI company, and this US Homeland Security order is a shopping ban plus a cleanup: civilian federal agencies may not buy its products and must remove them, along with third-party products built using DeepSeek. The BBC says it covers agencies such as Treasury, State and Justice, not defence, and took effect at the end of July, so October is when it became public. TechCrunch says DHS warned that data from government users could be accessible to Chinese authorities. That is a stated risk, and no actual misuse is described. Agencies can request exceptions. China's foreign ministry opposed \"overstretching the concept of national security\".",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "torchtpu",
   "headline": "Google opens TorchTPU to loosen Nvidia's grip",
   "facts": [
    "Open-sourced 20 Oct at PyTorch Conference",
    "Co-developed with Meta's PyTorch team",
    "Validated up to 8,000 TPUs, Google's claim",
    "Amazon TorchNeuron 19 Oct"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/ai-infrastructure/torchtpu-is-now-open-source-run-native-pytorch-on-tpus",
    "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/20/google-has-joined-amazon-in-attacking-nvidias-stronghold-with-ai-app-developers/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "Think of PyTorch as a common language for writing AI programs, and each AI chip as a machine that needs a translator to understand it. TorchTPU is such a translator: on 20 Oct Google open-sourced it so PyTorch programs run natively on its own TPU chips, with existing code needing \"minimal changes\", and says Meta's PyTorch team co-developed it. Amazon released TorchNeuron for its Trainium chips on 19 Oct. Google claims training was validated on up to 8,000 TPUs with near-linear scaling, meaning twice the chips gives close to twice the speed. Those numbers are Google's own, and TechCrunch, which frames both tools as challenges to Nvidia, notes developers are unlikely to leave it en masse.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  }
